{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And Jethro, Moses' father-in-law, took Zipporah, Moses' wife.</b> Surely it was not for nothing that Scripture specified the name of his wife and the names of his sons, for Jethro said to him: Go for the sake of your wife Zipporah, for ״כְּצִפּוֹר נוֹדֵד מִקִּנּוֹ כֵּן אִישׁ נוֹדֵד מִמְּקוֹמוֹ״ (Proverbs 27:8) — like a bird wandering from its nest, so a man wanders from his place — and he came to remind him of his wife's distress all the time she was wandering from her home. And if not for her sake — for perhaps a man does not feel so keenly the distress of his wife — go for the sake of your son Gershom, named ״כִּי גֵר הָיִיתִי בְּאֶרֶץ נָכְרִיָּה״ (Exodus 2:22) — for I was a stranger in a foreign land — and he came to remind him of the distress of children who do not sit at their father's table, for they are strangers, and he said to him: ״אַתָּה יָדַעְתָּ אֶת נֶפֶשׁ הַגֵּר כִּי גֵר הָיִיתָ גַּם אַתָּה״ (Exodus 23:9) — you know the soul of the stranger, for you too were a stranger. And if not for his sake, go for the sake of your son Eliezer, who was named ״כִּי אֱלֹהֵי אָבִי בְּעֶזְרִי״ (Exodus 18:4) — for the Elohim of my father was my help — and his name is as the name of his master, and it is as though you are receiving the face of the Shekhinah, for His name is within him. Therefore Scripture mentioned their names, for thus Jethro sent to him, that he should act for the sake of his wife who was like a bird wandering from her nest, and on account of the distress she suffered it is fitting to honor her and to go out toward her; and likewise on account of his son who was a stranger in a foreign land; and likewise on account of the name Eliezer, for through this it is as though he went out to meet Elohim. And what is stated, ״וְשֵׁם הָאֶחָד אֱלִיעֶזֶר״ (Exodus 18:4), concerning which our Sages of blessed memory (Yalkut Shimoni, Jethro, §268) said that the Holy One, blessed be He, said: 'In the future Eliezer will demand a red heifer, daughter of two years, a calf, daughter of its year' — this will be explained with the help of HaShem in the portion of Chukkat (Numbers 19:2)."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:21:05.128000240Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}